# TDD and formal verification

Use test-driven development for every behavior change.

1. Write a failing test that states the behavior.
2. Run it and confirm it fails for the reason you expect.
3. Write the code that makes that test pass.
4. Re-run that test and the nearest existing checks.

Always create or update a project-local formal verification skill when a change creates or alters a promise, unless a skill in `.cursor/skills/` already verifies that promise. Follow `/create-formal-verification-skill`. Do not weaken a property so a check passes. After merges that change verified code without re-running the check, follow `/maintain-formal-verification-skill`.
